@startuml
title Client: submit a move (GUI and REST share the facade)

actor Player
participant "Board.qml" as QML
participant TrainerBridge as Br
participant BoardModel as BM
actor "REST client" as Http
participant ClientApiServer as Rest
participant TrainerService as Svc
participant PuzzleSession as Ses
participant MoveValidator as Val
participant StatsStore as Stats

== GUI path ==
Player -> QML: click own piece, then target square
QML -> Br: squareClicked(row), twice
Br -> BM: setSelectedRow, squareAt
Br -> Svc: submitMove(sessionId, "e2e4")

== REST path ==
Http -> Rest: POST /sessions/{id}/moves, body move = e2e4
Rest -> Rest: ApiJson::moveFromBody (else 400)
Rest -> Svc: submitMove(sessionId, "e2e4")

== Common core, under the TrainerService mutex ==
Svc -> Ses: submit(uci)
Ses -> Val: check(position, uci, expected)
Val --> Ses: Correct, Wrong or Illegal
Ses -> Ses: play the move, auto-play the opponent reply
Ses --> Svc: MoveResult (fenAfterMove, opponentReply)
alt solved or failed
  Svc -> Stats: record(puzzle, solved)
  Svc -> Svc: close the session
end
note over Svc: after the mutex is released, the change listener queues refreshStats to the GUI thread
Svc --> Rest: MoveOutcome
Rest --> Http: 200 with verdict JSON (404 if the session is unknown)
Svc --> Br: MoveOutcome
Br -> BM: setFen(fenAfterMove), setLastMove
Br -> BM: after 400 ms, setFen(fen) with the opponent reply
Br --> QML: feedback banner and statistics
@enduml
